      "writtenOn": "2025-09-19T20:12:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I need to explicitly enable the configuration option that provides the `k_malloc` function. If I comment out the config `CONFIG_HEAP_MEM_POOL_SIZE\u003d1024`, I get a linker error:\n\n```\nld.lld: error: undefined symbol: k_malloc\n\u003e\u003e\u003e referenced by ap_events.c:23 (/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/ap_events.c:23)\n```\n\nAdded this comment:\n```\n# Size of the kernel heap memory pool, primarily used by k_malloc()\n# and k_free().\n```",
